WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.380
Okay, so can you connect Klein bottles together, and if so, what do you get? Well,

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.240
I take a Möbius loop

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:10.920
Right, I give a -

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:14.790
half twist, get a Möbius loop. What if I give it -

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:17.470
another half twist?

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:25.439
Turns out that's not a Möbius loop. It's two-sided. Give it yet another half twist. It becomes a Möbius loop.

00:00:31.809 --> 00:00:37.079
Probably the most famous Möbius loop has three half twists to it

00:00:39.129 --> 00:00:44.399
It's the recycle sign - and you can see there's 1, 2, 3 half twists to it.

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:47.520
That's a Möbius loop, just like

00:00:51.579 --> 00:00:54.359
that's a Möbius loop. To be a Möbius loop

00:00:55.059 --> 00:00:58.589
you have to be able to walk on all one side

00:00:59.109 --> 00:01:02.759
without crossing an edge. Yep. Ok, got that one

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:07.169
Oh, my fingers are blue from having tried to put blue

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:12.510
dye into a Klein bottle. Ignore that, they'll wash off in the next two or three weeks.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:15.180
So, I can make a three twist

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:21.509
Möbius loop. Can I do the same thing with a Klein bottle? What if I take a Klein bottle,

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:24.780
and add another Klein bottle to it?

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:32.549
Oh, I can go over the glass shop, get a scissors cut that there, cut that there, get another one and build - this.

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:40.500
Is this a Klein bottle? It's two Klein bottles welded together. Oh, let's get a -

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:45.360
pen. Okay, let's start over here and write the letter A,

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:48.210
and the letter B.

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:54.240
Well, let's start at A, going along here.

00:01:56.770 --> 00:02:04.140
Oh, I can't keep going. I'm on the inside of this part. Still on the inside, still on the inside, still on the inside.

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:16.330
Well, come out over here and I come back to A.

00:02:20.269 --> 00:02:25.779
So, I can go from A, all the way back to A but I never get to the letter B

00:02:27.709 --> 00:02:30.699
Meaning that this side here,

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:35.200
the A side, is different from the B side.

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:41.079
B and A are on different sides. 
- (Brady: So, Cliff, someone watching might be thinking)

00:02:41.079 --> 00:02:43.479
(oh, no. I can just run my finger
 directly from A to B, but - )

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:51.309
You're, you're cheating if you go like this and go bonk like that. No! We're talking about, we're talking about a

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:54.970
mathematical thing like this. Where, where, where -

00:02:56.060 --> 00:03:01.420
my glass blower had actually cut a hole here, so you can go, ziip - zip through it go around the inside.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:07.120
Nah, this is something - this is a figment of our - figment of our three-dimensional universe. Ignore that one.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:10.860
(Brady: That self-intersection doesn't count?)

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:15.540
That self-intersection doesn't count. From the outside here, Bzz! Now you're on the *bzz*

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:17.860
inside of this

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:21.429
Bzzz! Now you're on the outside of this and you're back there. So this

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:27.549
turns out to have two sides, and a hole there. This is homeomorphic to a torus.

00:03:27.859 --> 00:03:33.039
Okay, got that. What if I add another one to this? I'll go from here to here,

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:35.560
Here's three

00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:39.339
Klein bottles arranged. Well, let's try the same experiment.

00:03:40.609 --> 00:03:43.119
I'll write A over here,

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:48.010
B,

00:03:48.139 --> 00:03:50.139
And C.

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:55.900
Okay, triple Klein bottle go from A, 
*Bzzz*

00:03:56.299 --> 00:03:58.629
Over here. Now, I'm on the inside of B

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:02.290
...still on the inside...

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:04.750
I come out here,

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:07.830
Now I'm on the outside of C.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:09.880
Okay,

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:19.500
outside of C, go back here. Outside, outside, outside, outside. Oh look, I end up on the inside of A. Aah!

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:24.480
You go around the inside of A. I'm now right here, so, without

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:29.579
lifting the pen from the surface of the glass, I've gone from the

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:37.560
outside - from the outside over here over to the inside. This is one sided. Let's keep going.

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:43.560
I'm still on the inside of this one - I need - a millimeter away from here is where I'm trying...I see,

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:48.269
Still on the inside, still on the inside, I come around here,

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:55.410
I've hit the outside, I've hit B! Hot Diggity! Ah, cool! Now, I come around,

00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:59.159
And I'm on the outside, *glook* through there,

00:05:00.729 --> 00:05:08.729
now I'm on the inside of this, and I've reached the other side of the C surface. I stand that other side,

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:12.750
come out here, I am back to where I started.

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:19.529
I've covered the entire surface. An ant could walk on the entire surface of this,

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:22.800
just, you know, ignoring the,

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:25.500
little places where, you can't get through.

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:34.019
So this is a Klein bottle. It's one-sided. There's no edge. At no point is there sharp edge that the

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:37.769
caterpillar crawling the surface ever got cut on. 
(Brady: You could, )

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:44.250
(paint the whole thing by pouring paint over one side and the - )
- That's right, if I, if I hired a painter they could paint the

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:48.839
whole thing with one side, and one colour - piece of cake works like gangbusters!

